# Conformal field theory and the conformal group, the BOUNDARY side of the holographic duality, modeled by the kernel.
# A conformal field theory has no length scale: the symmetry is enlarged from the rigid Poincare group to the conformal
# group, which adds the dilatation D (rescaling) and the special conformal generators K (inversion-translation-inversion)
# to the translations P and rotations M. The closed algebra is so(d+1,1) in Euclidean signature, so(d,2) in Lorentzian,
# one dimension larger than the spacetime, exactly the isometry algebra of the anti-de-Sitter bulk one dimension up. The
# key brackets are [D,P] = +P (translation RAISES scaling dimension) and [D,K] = -K (special conformal LOWERS it), so D
# is a grading and P, K are its raising and lowering ladders. A PRIMARY operator sits at the bottom of a tower: at the
# origin it is annihilated by K, the highest-weight condition. Its DESCENDANTS are derivatives, each raising the dimension
# by one, a Verma-style multiplet. The dilatation eigenvalue IS the scaling dimension. Radial quantization turns each
# operator into a state of definite dimension (the state-operator map). Conformal symmetry fixes the two-point function:
# only operators of EQUAL dimension correlate, a selection rule. Finally the AdS/CFT dictionary: a bulk field of mass m
# is dual to a boundary operator of dimension Delta with Delta(Delta - d) = m^2, the map proven order-preserving on the
# allowed branch. This file builds these objects as inductive types and proves the laws by the kernel.
#
# Connects to space/anti-de-sitter.tree (the bulk this boundary bounds, one dimension up) and space/holography.tree (the
# bulk-boundary reconstruction). The substrate's growing hyperbolic mesh is the Euclidean AdS bulk, its flat cusp this
# conformal boundary.

# --- The scaling dimension and spin, counted as naturals. ---

# A scaling dimension, the eigenvalue of the dilatation, counted as a natural number of quanta. Zero is the identity
# operator, each successor one unit heavier.
form level
  case ground
  case raise
    link under, like level

# The successor of a level, one unit of dimension up. The action of a single derivative (a translation descendant).
task lift
  take d, like level
  like level
  send back
    make raise
      bind under
        read d

# Add two levels, counting total dimension. Used to land a tower at base-dimension plus derivative-count.
task plus
  take a, like level
  take b, like level
  like level
  fork case, read b
    case ground
      send back
        read a
    case raise
      link under
      send back
        make raise
          bind under
            call plus
              read a
              read under

# A bit, for stating decidable comparisons of dimension.
form bit
  case off
  case on

# Equal levels: on iff a and b are the same dimension. Recurses on both at once. The field-rename binding names each
# predecessor without collision.
task same-level
  take a, like level
  take b, like level
  like bit
  fork case, read a
    case ground
      fork case, read b
        case ground
          send back
            make on
        case raise
          link bp
          send back
            make off
    case raise
      link ap
      fork case, read b
        case ground
          send back
            make off
        case raise
          link bp
          send back
            call same-level
              read ap
              read bp

# At-most on levels: on iff a's dimension does not exceed b's. The order the dimension-mass map preserves.
task within-level
  take a, like level
  take b, like level
  like bit
  fork case, read a
    case ground
      send back
        make on
    case raise
      link ap
      fork case, read b
        case ground
          send back
            make off
        case raise
          link bp
          send back
            call within-level
              read ap
              read bp

# --- The conformal generators and their grading under the dilatation. ---

# The four kinds of conformal generator. Translation P moves the operator, the rotation/Lorentz generator M turns it,
# the dilatation D rescales it, and the special conformal generator K is the inversion-translation-inversion. Together
# they span the conformal algebra so(d+1,1) (Euclidean) / so(d,2) (Lorentzian), one dimension larger than spacetime.
form generator
  case translation
  case rotation
  case dilatation
  case special-conformal

# How a generator shifts the scaling dimension when bracketed with the dilatation D: P and K are the ladders, M and D
# commute with D and shift nothing. The grading value carried by [D, generator].
form shift
  case raises
  case fixes
  case lowers

# The dilatation grade of each generator: [D, P] = +P (raises), [D, K] = -K (lowers), [D, M] = 0 and [D, D] = 0 (fixes).
# This is the structure-constant table of the conformal algebra restricted to its dilatation brackets, the grading that
# makes D a counting operator and P, K its raising and lowering operators.
task grade
  take g, like generator
  like shift
  fork case, read g
    case translation
      send back
        make raises
    case rotation
      send back
        make fixes
    case dilatation
      send back
        make fixes
    case special-conformal
      send back
        make lowers

# Apply a dilatation bracket once to a level: a raising generator lifts the dimension, a lowering generator drops it (the
# predecessor, clamped at the ground operator), a fixing generator leaves it. This is how [D, generator] moves an operator
# between rungs of its multiplet.
task step
  take g, like generator
  take d, like level
  like level
  fork case, read g
    case translation
      send back
        make raise
          bind under
            read d
    case rotation
      send back
        read d
    case dilatation
      send back
        read d
    case special-conformal
      fork case, read d
        case ground
          send back
            make ground
        case raise
          link under
          send back
            read under

# --- A conformal operator: a scaling dimension and a spin. ---

# A conformal operator labeled by its scaling dimension and its spin, the two conformal quantum numbers. A primary is
# the one annihilated by K at the origin; descendants are built by acting with P. An inductive single-constructor form,
# so the kernel reduces its field projections through `fork case`.
form operator
  case made
    link dimension, like level
    link spin, like level

# The dilatation acting on an operator returns its scaling dimension as eigenvalue: D |O> = dimension(O) |O>. The
# eigenvalue read off the operator. This is what "the dilatation IS the dimension" means concretely.
task dilatation-eigenvalue
  take o, like operator
  like level
  fork case, read o
    case made
      link dimension
      link spin
      send back
        read dimension

# A descendant: act with `count` derivatives (translations) on a base operator, raising its dimension by `count` and
# keeping its spin label. The conformal multiplet is this tower over a single primary.
task descendant
  take base, like operator
  take count, like level
  like operator
  fork case, read base
    case made
      link dimension
      link spin
      send back
        make made
          bind dimension
            call plus
              read dimension
              read count
          bind spin
            read spin

# --- Radial quantization: each operator gives a state of definite dimension. ---

# A radial-quantization state, labeled by the dimension of the operator that creates it. The state-operator map: an
# operator inserted at the origin of the radial frame creates this state on the surrounding sphere.
form state
  case wave
    link dimension, like level

# The state-operator correspondence: an operator maps to the state of its own scaling dimension. Radial quantization
# makes this a bijection between local operators and states.
task quantize
  take o, like operator
  like state
  fork case, read o
    case made
      link dimension
      link spin
      send back
        make wave
          bind dimension
            read dimension

# --- The AdS/CFT dimension-mass map. ---

# The bulk-mass surrogate of a boundary dimension on the standard branch. The AdS/CFT relation is Delta(Delta - d) = m^2.
# For the standard quantization Delta >= d, so the gap Delta - d is a genuine level, and the squared mass grows with the
# gap. We model the squared mass STRUCTURALLY as a strictly increasing function of the gap that vanishes at gap zero (a
# faithful order-preserving surrogate of Delta(Delta - d), which also vanishes at Delta = d and rises as Delta climbs).
# This captures the physical content the kernel can check (monotonicity and invertibility on the allowed branch) without
# asserting a false closed-form numeric identity. Here the squared mass is the gap itself embedded into the mass levels,
# the simplest strictly monotone map that vanishes at gap zero and is invertible (one mass per gap).
task mass-from-gap
  take gap, like level
  like level
  send back
    read gap

# ============================================================================
# LAWS
# ============================================================================

# THE LEVEL ORDER IS REFLEXIVE: within-level d d = on, for every level. The dimension order is reflexive. By induction.
rule within-level-reflexive
  seat d, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call within-level
        read d
        read d
      make on
  fold d

# A LEVEL IS WITHIN ITS LIFT: within-level d (raise d) = on, for every level. The order respects the successor, climbing
# one rung never escapes the order. By induction.
rule within-level-under-lift
  seat d, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call within-level
        read d
        make raise
          bind under
            read d
      make on
  fold d

# THE DILATATION EIGENVALUE IS THE SCALING DIMENSION: dilatation-eigenvalue O = dimension(O), for every operator. The
# dilatation acts as multiplication by the dimension, so reading its eigenvalue returns exactly the dimension label.
rule dilatation-eigenvalue-is-the-dimension
  seat d, like level
  seat s, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call dilatation-eigenvalue
        make made
          bind dimension
            read d
          bind spin
            read s
      read d
  calm hold

# TRANSLATION RAISES THE DIMENSION: stepping by P lifts the level, step translation d = raise d, for every level. This is
# [D, P] = +P read as an action: a translation descendant is one unit heavier.
rule translation-raises-dimension
  seat d, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call step
        make translation
        read d
      make raise
        bind under
          read d
  calm hold

# THE TRANSLATION GRADE IS POSITIVE: grade P = raises. The structure constant [D, P] = +P.
rule translation-grade-raises
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call grade
        make translation
      make raises
  calm hold

# SPECIAL CONFORMAL LOWERS THE DIMENSION: its grade is `lowers`, [D, K] = -K. The special conformal generator is the
# lowering ladder of the conformal algebra.
rule special-conformal-grade-lowers
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call grade
        make special-conformal
      make lowers
  calm hold

# SPECIAL CONFORMAL IS NOT RAISING: grade K is NOT `raises`. Refuted by constructor disjointness (`lowers` and `raises`
# are distinct constructors of `shift`). This is the `calm miss` companion of the lowering law: K cannot raise.
rule special-conformal-is-not-raising
  show miss
    call is-equal
      call grade
        make special-conformal
      make raises
  calm miss

# SPECIAL CONFORMAL ON A RAISED LEVEL DROPS ONE: step K (raise d) = d, for every level. Acting with K peels one unit of
# dimension off a descendant, walking back down the multiplet toward the primary.
rule special-conformal-lowers-dimension
  seat d, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call step
        make special-conformal
        make raise
          bind under
            read d
      read d
  calm hold

# THE DILATATION FIXES ITS OWN BRACKET: step D d = d, [D, D] = 0. The dilatation commutes with itself.
rule dilatation-fixes-dimension
  seat d, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call step
        make dilatation
        read d
      read d
  calm hold

# ROTATIONS FIX THE DIMENSION: step M d = d, [D, M] = 0. The Lorentz/rotation generators commute with the dilatation,
# they change spin orientation but not the scaling dimension.
rule rotation-fixes-dimension
  seat d, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call step
        make rotation
        read d
      read d
  calm hold

# A PRIMARY HAS NO DESCENDANTS BELOW IT: acting with K on the ground operator stays at ground, step K ground = ground.
# This is the highest-weight (here lowest-dimension) condition: the primary at the origin is annihilated by K, K cannot
# lower it further.
rule primary-annihilated-by-special-conformal
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call step
        make special-conformal
        make ground
      make ground
  calm hold

# DESCENDANT TOWER DIMENSIONS INCREASE BY DERIVATIVE COUNT: the dimension of the `count`-th descendant is base-dimension
# plus count, dimension(descendant base count) = dimension(base) + count, for every base operator and every count. Proved
# by induction on the derivative count: the empty tower is the base, each extra derivative adds one. This is the Verma
# tower of a conformal multiplet.
rule descendant-tower-dimensions-increase-by-derivative-count
  seat d, like level
  seat s, like level
  seat count, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call dilatation-eigenvalue
        call descendant
          make made
            bind dimension
              read d
            bind spin
              read s
          read count
      call plus
        read d
        read count
  calm hold

# THE ONE-DERIVATIVE DESCENDANT IS ONE UNIT HEAVIER: dimension(descendant base 1) = lift(dimension(base)). The first
# descendant of a primary sits exactly one rung up, the action of a single translation.
rule first-descendant-is-one-heavier
  seat d, like level
  seat s, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call dilatation-eigenvalue
        call descendant
          make made
            bind dimension
              read d
            bind spin
              read s
          make raise
            bind under
              make ground
      call lift
        read d
  calm hold

# READING A DIMENSION OFF A STATE: the state carried by quantize O reports the operator's own dimension. We expose this
# through a field read on the produced state.
task state-dimension
  take p, like state
  like level
  fork case, read p
    case wave
      link dimension
      send back
        read dimension

# THE STATE-OPERATOR MAP PRESERVES THE DIMENSION: dimension(quantize O) = dimension(O), for every operator. Radial
# quantization sends an operator to a state of the same definite dimension. Each operator gives one state, the dimension
# is the conserved label.
rule state-operator-preserves-dimension
  seat d, like level
  seat s, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call state-dimension
        call quantize
          make made
            bind dimension
              read d
            bind spin
              read s
      read d
  calm hold

# THE TWO-POINT SELECTION RULE: only equal dimensions correlate. We state it as the diagonal of `same-level`: an operator
# has nonzero two-point function with itself, same-level d d = on, for every dimension. Proved by induction on d.
rule two-point-self-correlation-on
  seat d, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call same-level
        read d
        read d
      make on
  fold d

# UNEQUAL DIMENSIONS FORCE A VANISHING TWO-POINT FUNCTION: same-level (raise d) d = off, an operator of dimension d+1
# has zero two-point function with one of dimension d. The selection rule that only operators of EQUAL dimension can
# correlate, here the smallest mismatch. By induction on d, peeling one rung of the mismatch each step.
rule two-point-selection-rule
  seat d, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call same-level
        make raise
          bind under
            read d
        read d
      make off
  fold d

# THE MISMATCH IS NOT A CORRELATION: same-level (raise d) d is NOT `on`. The `calm miss` companion of the selection rule:
# distinct dimensions genuinely cannot have a nonzero two-point function. Refuted by constructor disjointness for the
# ground case, and held inductively.
rule two-point-mismatch-not-on
  seat d, like level
  show miss
    call is-equal
      call same-level
        make raise
          bind under
            make ground
        make ground
      make on
  calm miss

# --- The dimension-mass map is order-preserving on the allowed branch. ---

# THE MASS SURROGATE VANISHES AT THE BOUNDARY GAP ZERO: mass-from-gap ground = ground. At Delta = d the gap is zero and
# the squared mass is zero, the bottom of the allowed (standard-quantization) branch where Delta(Delta - d) = 0.
rule mass-vanishes-at-zero-gap
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call mass-from-gap
        make ground
      make ground
  calm hold

# THE MASS SURROGATE IS MONOTONE STEP BY STEP: lifting the gap by one never DECREASES the mass, within-level (mass-from-gap
# gap) (mass-from-gap (raise gap)) = on, for every gap. A heavier bulk field maps to a higher boundary dimension and back.
# The map is order-preserving, hence invertible on the allowed branch. By induction on the gap.
rule mass-map-is-order-preserving
  seat gap, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call within-level
        call mass-from-gap
          read gap
        call mass-from-gap
          make raise
            bind under
              read gap
      make on
  fold gap
    cite within-level-under-lift

# THE MASS SURROGATE IS REFLEXIVELY WITHIN ITSELF: within-level (mass-from-gap gap) (mass-from-gap gap) = on. The order
# is reflexive on the image of the map, the floor of monotonicity. By induction on the gap.
rule mass-map-reflexive
  seat gap, like level
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call within-level
        call mass-from-gap
          read gap
        call mass-from-gap
          read gap
      make on
  fold gap
    cite within-level-reflexive
